ings', 'text': 'NIKE INC - ON APRIL 6, 2020, ENTERED INTO COMMITTED CREDIT FACILITY AGREEMENT WITH A SYNDICATE OF BANKS WHICH PROVIDES FOR UP TO $2 BILLION OF BORROWINGS.NIKE INC - NEW FACILITY MATURES ON APRIL 5, 2021.'}{'symbol': 'PRGO', 'date': '2020-04-08 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Perrigo Expects Q1 Sales Were About $1.3 Billion', 'text': 'PERRIGO ANNOUNCES PRELIMINARY UNAUDITED FIRST QUARTER 2020 NET SALES AND PROVIDES FIRST QUARTER OPERATING INCOME RANGE.SEES Q1 SALES ABOUT $1.3 BILLION.SEES Q1 SALES UP 14 PERCENT.EXPECT Q1 WORLDWIDE CONSUMER NET SALES WERE ABOUT $1.1 BILLION .ESTIMATED Q1 GAAP OPERATING INCOME OF $140 MILLION TO $145 MILLION AND NON-GAAP ("ADJUSTED") OPERATING INCOME OF $220 MILLION TO $225 MILLION.FISCAL YEAR 2020 GUIDANCE REMAINS UNCHANGED GIVEN UNCERTAINTY IN CURRENT OPERATING ENVIRONMENT RELATED TO COVID-19.PERRIGO - DURING Q1, CONTINUED TO EXPERIENCE STRONG GROWTH ACROSS ALL BUSINESS UNITS.BENEFITED FROM A DRAMATIC SURGE IN DEMAND IN MARCH RELATED TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.PRELIM Q1 ORGANIC NET SALES HIGHER BY 11%.Q1 REVENUE VIEW $1.26 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'PSX', 'date': '2020-04-08 15:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Phillips 66 Reports Unit Shutdown at Ponca City, Oklahoma Refinery on April 2', 'text': 'PONCA CITY, OKLAHOMA REFINERY REPORTS UNIT SHUTDOWN, EMISSIONS OF CARBON MONOXIDE ON APRIL 2.'}{'symbol': 'PVH', 'date': '2020-04-08 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Pvh Corp - Furloughs, Decreased Working Hours And Salary Reductions In North America', 'text': "PVH CORP. ANNOUNCES BUSINESS UPDATE RELATING TO COVID-19 OUTBREAK.PVH CORP - BOARD OF DIRECTORS COMPENSATION SUSPENDED.PVH CORP - FURLOUGHS, DECREASED WORKING HOURS AND SALARY REDUCTIONS IN NORTH AMERICA.PVH CORP - ADDITIONALLY, APPROXIMATELY 250 SENIOR LEADERS AND EXECUTIVES GLOBALLY WILL EXPERIENCE SALARY REDUCTIONS OF UP TO 50%.PVH CORP - FURLOUGHS WILL BE UNPAID AND ASSOCIATES WHO HAVE THEIR HOURS REDUCED WILL HAVE THEIR PAY REDUCED PROPORTIONALLY TO THEIR HOUR REDUCTIONS